body:
I have a simple two-layer network and it crashes on the forward pass.

```python
import torch.nn as nn

class M(nn.Module):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
        self.fc1 = nn.Linear(20, 30)
        self.fc2 = nn.Linear(40, 10)

    def forward(self, x):
        return self.fc2(self.fc1(x))
```

The second layer expects 40 features but the first produces 30.
